Here is a rewritten, agent-ready prompt. It locks in every decision that a coding agent would otherwise guess at, enumerates edge cases, defines the allowed/disallowed action surface, and specifies exactly how the agent must verify its own work. I've also adapted it to your Firefox-only, zero-cost constraint, which changes several technical details from your original prompt.

