# DATA CONTRACTS

## types.ts

```ts
export interface Skill {
  id: string;          // e.g. "opsx:propose" (namespace:name)
  namespace: string;   // e.g. "opsx"
  name: string;        // e.g. "propose"
  description: string; // one-line human-readable
  file: string;        // relative path on CDN, e.g. "skills/opsx/propose/SKILL.md"
}

export interface SkillRegistry {
  version: string;     // ISO timestamp
  skills: Skill[];
}

export type Message =
  | { type: "GET_REGISTRY"; forceRefresh?: boolean }
  | { type: "GET_SKILL_CONTENT"; skillId: string }
  | { type: "COPY_TO_CLIPBOARD"; text: string }
  | { type: "GET_STATUS" };

export type MessageResponse<T = unknown> =
  | { ok: true; data: T }
  | { ok: false; error: string; code: ErrorCode };

export type ErrorCode =
  | "NETWORK_ERROR"
  | "NOT_FOUND"
  | "CACHE_MISS"
  | "CLIPBOARD_DENIED"
  | "INVALID_RESPONSE"
  | "UNKNOWN";
```

# FUNCTIONAL REQUIREMENTS (TESTABLE)

FR-1. The extension declares `clipboardWrite`, `storage`, and
      host permission for the CDN domain only.

FR-2. The content script is injected ONLY on these origins:
      - https://chat.openai.com/*
      - https://chatgpt.com/*
      - https://gemini.google.com/*
      - https://chat.qwen.ai/*
      - https://qwen.ai/*
      - https://www.perplexity.ai/*

FR-3. The content script detects the active chat input element.
      Support both `<textarea>` and `[contenteditable="true"]`.
      Use a MutationObserver to handle SPA route changes.

FR-4. When the user types `/` as the FIRST character of the input
      value, the command palette appears anchored above the input.

FR-5. The palette filters the cached skill registry using
      `id.startsWith(query)` as primary and a fuzzy fallback
      (case-insensitive substring match on id + description).

FR-6. Keyboard navigation inside the palette:
      - ArrowDown / ArrowUp: move selection
      - Enter: select highlighted skill
      - Escape: close palette, do not clear input
      - Tab: select highlighted skill (same as Enter)

FR-7. On selection, the extension MUST:
      a) Clear the palette from the DOM.
      b) Clear the leading `/query` text from the chat input.
      c) Fetch the SKILL.md content (from cache or CDN).
      d) Write the content to the clipboard.
      e) Show a non-blocking toast: "Skill copied. Paste into your prompt."
         The toast auto-dismisses after 4 seconds.
      f) Log the outcome to the debug logger.

FR-8. The background event page:
      - Serves GET_REGISTRY from browser.storage.local if cached
        and not expired (TTL: 6 hours).
      - On cache miss, fetches from the CDN, validates the JSON
        shape, and writes to storage.
      - Serves GET_SKILL_CONTENT from an in-memory LRU cache
        (max 20 entries) before hitting the network.
      - NEVER touches the clipboard directly.

FR-9. The popup displays:
      - Registry version + last refresh timestamp
      - A "Refresh skills" button (forces a re-fetch)
      - A "Clear cache" button
      - A short link to the skill repo (configurable constant)

FR-10. All network requests use `AbortController` with a 10-second
       timeout. A timeout is treated as NETWORK_ERROR.

FR-11. The extension must function offline for skills already cached.
       If the registry is cached and the network is down, the palette
       still works for known skills.

# EDGE CASES (MUST BE HANDLED)

E-1.  User types `/` in the middle of a sentence → palette does NOT open.
E-2.  Chat input is a contenteditable div whose textContent contains
      non-breaking spaces → normalize before checking for leading `/`.
E-3.  SPA navigation changes the chat input element → re-attach listeners.
E-4.  User pastes text into the input while the palette is open → close it.
E-5.  Clipboard write is denied by Firefox → show an inline error toast:
      "Clipboard blocked. Click the page first, then try again."
E-6.  Skill markdown contains Unicode (emoji, CJK) → preserve byte-for-byte.
E-7.  Skill markdown is empty → do not copy, show error toast.
E-8.  Registry JSON is malformed → discard, keep the old cache, log error.
E-9.  CDN returns 404 for a skill file → show "Skill unavailable" toast.
E-10. Two rapid selections → deduplicate; only the latest wins.
E-11. Palette must not appear when the user is inside a code block
      in the chat input (contenteditable with `pre` ancestor).
E-12. If the registry is empty (no skills), the palette shows a single
      row: "No skills available. Refresh from the popup."
E-13. If the extension loads on a page where the input is inside a
      shadow DOM, do NOT attempt to pierce it; log a debug warning.
E-14. Long skill IDs must not overflow the palette; use ellipsis.
E-15. All UI text must be selectable and readable at 100% zoom.

# ERROR HANDLING POLICY

- Never throw uncaught errors into the console in production builds.
- Every network call must be wrapped in try/catch.
- Every message handler must return a typed MessageResponse.
- On unrecoverable errors, fail silently for the user but log to the
  debug logger (enabled only when `browser.storage.local.debug === true`).

